## Corpus expansion (documents 31–58)

The license-summary table above and the attributions below enumerate the
**original 30-document core corpus**. The corpus was later expanded to **58
documents** (see [`docs/journal/02-data-expansion.md`](docs/journal/02-data-expansion.md)).
The per-source publisher, license, and provenance for **every** document —
original and expansion — are recorded in each `data/raw/<source_id>/manifest.json`.

Expansion sources are predominantly **US Government works** (e.g. CRS, DTIC, NPS —
US public domain). They also include **publicly-released analyses from
organizations such as ICRC, CNAS, and RUSI that retain their own copyright**;
these are included for non-commercial academic research. For the redistribution
terms of any specific expansion document, consult its `manifest.json` and the
original publisher.

